Interpretation: WGS is memory-heavy but not at the DRAM ceiling. The main resource constraint is the large per-CTA shared-memory/register footprint. Lowering FT_T to 32 reduced the tile but materially regressed all scored batches (see moe_wgs_ft32_v1); a redesign must preserve weight reuse and scheduling efficiency while changing resource allocation.

Profiler setup history: first run used an old diagnostic wrapper and failed before kernel launch because it expected `_finish_experts`; second run reached the kernel but Nsight's default clock locking was denied by Modal; corrected driver is `dev/modal/drv_moe_wgs_ncu.py` and the successful run used `--clock-control none`.
